      "textEn": "407\n\nIn the salt sea, it mixes. Those who come to bathe in the river are considered very lucky. It is not difficult for them to obtain the fruits of performing great sacrifices like Rajasuya and Ashwamedha on every step.\nIt is not difficult. Meaning: Even now, where the Ganges River meets the saline waters of the Bay of Bengal, that place is called Ganga\nSagar. In the months of January-February, on the occasion of Makar-Sankranti, even today, thousands of people come here to bathe with the desire to attain liberation, and in reality, they attain liberation,\nwhose confirmation has been done here. Those who take a bath in the Ganges at any time, it is not difficult for them to receive the fruits of great sacrifices like Ashwamedha and Rajasuya. Even today, most people in India are willing to bathe in the Ganges,\nand there are many places where they can bathe. In Prayag (Allahabad),\nEvery year in the month of January, millions of people gather at the confluence of the Ganga and Yamuna rivers to bathe.\nAre. After this, they bathe in the confluence of the Bay of Bengal and the Ganges.\nFor the people of India, this is a special facility that they can take a bath in the Ganges at many pilgrimage sites. And other rivers and streams, year after year, are numerous, the descendants of the mountain, hundreds of thousands. 10. Meaning of the word\n\nOther—other many; Ch—also; Nadah—rivers; Nadyah—small rivers; Ch—and; Varsha—year after year; Santi—are;\nMany—of many kinds; Meru-adi-giri-dhitarah—the daughters of Meru and other mountains; Shatashah—hundreds. Many small and big rivers originate from the peak of Mount Meru. These rivers are like the daughters of mountains,\nand they flow in hundreds of streams in various lands.\nThere, India itself is the year, the field of action, and the other eight years are the places of enjoyment of the merits of the heavenly beings, and the Bhoumas are the stations of the heavenly abode.\nThey describe it. 11. Meanin